    },
    "sources": [
      {
        "source_id": "beall_2016",
        "page": 1,
        "quote": "Don Stookey (Figure 1) was a well-known and highly respected scientist at Corning Incorporated, formerly Corning Glass Works, for 50 years (1940–1990)."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "stookey_invented_fotalite",
    "source": "stookey_s_donald",
    "type": "invented",
    "target": "fotalite",
    "sources": [
      {
        "source_id": "beall_2016",
        "page": 1,
        "quote": "His early work on dense opal glasses and photosensitive precipitation of gold and silver in glass led to an amazing series of inventions: Fotalite®, a photosensitive opal"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "stookey_invented_fotoform",
    "source": "stookey_s_donald",
    "type": "invented",
    "target": "fotoform",
    "sources": [
      {
        "source_id": "beall_2016",
        "page": 3,
        "quote": "This new photo-etchable material was called Fotoform®"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "stookey_invented_fotoceram",
    "source": "stookey_s_donald",
    "type": "invented",
    "target": "fotoceram",
    "sources": [
      {
        "source_id": "beall_2016",
        "page": 3,
        "quote": "This first glass–ceramic, called Fotoceram®, was predominantly crystalline (lithium disilicate) and stronger than Fotoform ®"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "stookey_invented_pyroceram",
    "source": "stookey_s_donald",
    "type": "invented",
    "target": "pyroceram",
    "sources": [
      {
        "source_id": "beall_2016",
        "page": 1,
        "quote": "and TiO2-nucleated Pyroceram™ products including missile nosecones and oven-proof cookware."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "stookey_invented_corningware",
    "source": "stookey_s_donald",
    "type": "invented",
    "target": "corningware",
    "sources": [
      {
        "source_id": "beall_2016",
        "page": 1,
        "quote": "including Corningware® cookware"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "stookey_invented_photochromic",
    "source": "stookey_s_donald",
    "type": "invented",
    "target": "photochromic_glass",
    "sources": [
      {
        "source_id": "beall_2016",
        "page": 1,
        "quote": "Don was able to demonstrate a clear photochromic glass that showed reversible darkening for thousands of cycles."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "stookey_invented_polychromatic",
    "source": "stookey_s_donald",
    "type": "invented",
    "target": "polychromatic_glass",
    "sources": [
      {
        "source_id": "beall_2016",
        "page": 1,
        "quote": "He went on to invent a full-color polychromatic glass, capable of yielding a permanent patterned and monolithic stained glass."
      }
    ]
  },
